[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit"]
[Variation "Queen's Gambit Declined: Austrian Defense"]
[ECO "D06"]
[Character "positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "open-the-centre"]
[Kind "sideline"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 c5 3. cxd5 { Opens the c-file and clears the way for the knight on c3 to hit the queen. } 3... Qxd5
4. Nf3 { Develops and prepares Nc3 so White gains time on the queen. } 4... cxd4
5. Nc3 { Hits the queen and gains time. } 5... Qa5
6. Nxd4 { Takes the pawn back with a developing move. } 6... Nf6
7. Nb3 { Hits the queen again and steps away from the pin and from exchanges. } 7... Qc7
8. e4 { Takes the centre now that Black has wasted time on the queen. Plan: develop the bishops, castle, and keep the pawns on e4 and d-file open. } *
